/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report"
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://api.cireweddings.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.cireweddings.com; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; report-uri https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report; report-to csp-endpoint

/claim*
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# Long-cache the immutable, content-hashed Astro bundles, the self-hosted font
# files included. Every path under /_astro/ carries a content hash in the
# filename, so a year-long cache is unconditionally safe: a changed file is a
# new URL, never the same one with different bytes.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# One ENFORCED policy: the browser blocks whatever it does not allow and
# reports each block to cire-api's first-party collector (`POST /api/csp-report`
# — public, creds-less, 204-always). The organiser portal's policy
# (`cire/host/public/_headers`) is the same bar `img-src`, which there admits
# any `https:` image for the registry's shop link picker; this portal has no
# such picker, so it enforces the tight list and needs no report-only twin.
# Before changing the policy, walk the dev tier with its collector's logs open
# (`wiki/cire/cire-development.md`, "Portal security headers").
#
# THIS FILE IS THE PRODUCTION POLICY. The build rewrites the copy in `dist/`
# (`src/lib/tier-headers.ts`): every `https://api.cireweddings.com` above
# becomes the origin of the `PUBLIC_CIRE_API_URL` the bundle was built with, so
# the dev tier allows and reports to its own API, and a local
# `wrangler pages dev dist` build allows the local one. Write only the
# production origin here; the build fails if this file stops naming it, or if
# the origin it writes appears in no client script.
#
# NO GOOGLE FONTS in `style-src` or `font-src`: `astro.config.mjs` downloads
# Schibsted Grotesk and Cormorant Garamond at build time via
# `fontProviders.google()`, and none of the three page shells links
# fonts.googleapis.com. It matters most on `/claim`, which is opened straight
# from an emailed invite: a Google stylesheet there would tell Google about
# every vendor who followed the link, before rendering a word.
#
# `script-src 'unsafe-inline'` is load-bearing: every built page carries three
# inline scripts — the theme-boot script (`THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT`, `is:inline` on
# all three shells so it can run before first paint), and Astro's own island
# loader and `astro-island` definition. The island chunks they load are
# `/_astro/*`, covered by 'self'.
#
# Other differences from `cire/host/public/_headers`, audited from source:
#   - No `blob:` in `img-src`: no cropper, no object URLs (`data:` is kept for
#     inline SVG data URIs).
#   - `connect-src` is cire-api only. Sign-in is a top-level redirect through
#     cire/api's OIDC leg and account management links out to musubi — both
#     navigations, which no `connect-src` governs.
#
# On avatars: `AccountAvatar` renders the OIDC `picture` claim, which can point
# at ANY https host — it is unvalidated at every hop between osn-api and here,
# so the sink (`httpsAvatarUrl`) is what enforces the scheme. `img-src` allows
# no avatar host, so the browser blocks the request and files a report, and
# `AccountAvatar` shows the initial instead. OSN hosts no avatars yet (osn-api
# writes `avatarUrl` null on registration and on erasure, and has no update
# path), so nothing populates the claim. Add OSN's avatar host here when it
# exists: englishstventures/osn#1207.
#
# The `/claim*` rule above only overrides `Referrer-Policy` (a claim token rides
# in the URL); Cloudflare merges the rules, so that path keeps the CSP header.
